# Before writing or changing music, read music/README.md (style, moods, format).
title    Badlands
composer Claude
about    Red mesas at dusk: a whistled flute in A minor over the old Andalusian walk down (Am G F E), its echo coming back off the canyon walls a dotted eighth later, a picked guitar and an upright bass. When something is near, a woodblock gallops over a low tom; a trumpet takes the tune into a fight, and a ghostly choir and gong come for a guardian.
tempo    84
beats    4
steps    4
reverb   0.45

# moods (music/README.md)
# mood explore:  lead echo guitar bass pad
# mood treasure: guitar pad wonder
# mood sense:    block toms shaker bass pad
# mood rise:     sense lead echo guitar kick snare
# mood fight:    rise -echo -shaker -guitar -block trumpet brass drive war crash
# mood boss:     fight -lead choir gong

voice lead     flute     vol=0.6  pan=-0.1 rev=0.5
voice echo     flute     vol=0.2  pan=0.5  rev=0.7
voice trumpet  trumpet   vol=0.60 pan=0.15 oct=-1 att=0.025 rel=0.12 rev=0.3
voice guitar   guitar    vol=0.55 pan=0.3
voice bass     upright   vol=0.75
voice pad      strings   vol=0.22 pan=-0.3 center=A3 att=0.5 rel=0.8
voice wonder   celesta   vol=0.38 pan=-0.3 rev=0.6
voice block    block     vol=0.4  pan=0.35
voice toms     tomlo     vol=0.55 pan=-0.2
voice shaker   shaker    vol=0.3  pan=0.25
voice kick     kick      vol=0.55
voice snare    snare     vol=0.38 pan=0.1
voice brass    brass     vol=0.42 pan=-0.25 gate=0.65 center=E4 att=0.018 rel=0.09 rev=0.22
voice crash    crash     vol=0.28 pan=0.2
voice choir    voices    vol=0.3  center=A3 att=0.5 rel=0.8
voice gong     gong      vol=0.3  pan=-0.3

# Combat-only motion: tight low ostinato and accented battle drums, at the same tempo.
voice drive    guitar    vol=0.58 pan=0.3 gate=0.55 rev=0.2
voice war      bodhran   vol=0.6  pan=-0.15 rev=0.2

# Am G F E twice; the motif (A B C E D) bends over the walk down
pattern A
